The attached image displays confocal microscopy results of skeletal muscle 24 hours after intramuscular injection, illustrating Nano-11's role in inducing inflammation and cellular uptake. The top row, showing Nano-11 combined with ovalbumin (Nano-11+OVA), reveals recruited Mac-2+ monocytes, MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, and 1A8+ neutrophils, with Nano-11 (red) visibly internalized by these cells. The bottom row, representing OVA injection alone, exhibits minimal inflammatory cell presence. This demonstrates Nano-11's ability to trigger local immune cell recruitment and facilitate antigen delivery to these cells, crucial for its adjuvant properties.